#chip 16F1829, 8

'Repeat For test (Change 1654): If X > 250 with the condition FALSE (variables pre-set before the loop). When a condition is true its body runs uncounted, by design, so the loop runs slightly long.
'Expect: compiles, and the whole Repeat For construct runs exactly 40,000 clock cycles
'(checked by simulating the generated assembly instruction by instruction)

#option explicit
Dim Flag As Bit
Dim Cnt As Byte
Dim X As Byte
Dim Y As Byte
Flag = 1
X = 200
Y = 1
Cnt = 0
Repeat For 20 ms
    If X > 250 Then
        Y = 1
    End If
End Repeat
Do
Loop
